            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0425" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/931</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-09-20T15:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 20, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 22, 7 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>236. Department’s telegram September 18, 5 p.m. With reference to Germany’s
                    proposition about neutralization of African colonies <pb facs="0426" n="112"
                        xml:id="pg112"/> lying in conventional free-trade zone, Germany wishes the
                    United States to act as messenger merely, to convey proposition to other
                    powers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
